---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
    <div
        data-home-lang="en"
        class="flex flex-col gap-4 lg:text-xl md:text-lg w-full text-left dark:text-gray-100 transition-colors"
    >
        <p>
            Hi! This is SmokingPuddle58, a graduate from Dept. of Mathematics of
            HKUST, and also a staff of HKUST.
        </p>
        <p>
            I'm a rhythm game enjoyer, especially maimaiDX and sometimes,
            Chunithm with friends. I was a osu!std enjoyer but I am not touching
            that anymore.
        </p>
        <p>
            This is my personal blog page, and I try not make this page too
            technical. Work is already tiring, so why write too many regarding
            programming?
        </p>
        <p>
            In this blog, I will put some personal things, probably something
            related to daily life, and in some cases, technical things that is
            used as a reminder and might help some other peoples.
        </p>
        <p>
            BTW, if you are looking for some details regarding to this site,
            probably you can take a look at <a href="/en/colophon">Colophon</a> page.
        </p>
        <p>So anyways, welcome to my page, and take your time here. Enjoy!</p>
    </div>

    <div
        class="flex flex-col items-center w-full dark:text-gray-100 transition-colors text-left"
    >
        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-horizontal gap-2 flex-wrap container"></div>
        <div
            class="rounded-lg border-2 border-gray-200 p-5 w-full m-5 bg-white dark:bg-slate-700 dark:text-gray-100 transition-colors"
        >
            <span id="description" class="lg:text-xl md:text-lg">Fun Facts</span
            >
            <div class="lg:text-lg md:text-md">
                <br />
                1. The name "SmokingPuddle58" comes from the Xbox default username.
                Which now I also uses for Minecraft.
                <br /><br />
                2. I have many different nicknames, being called by different people.
                These include "Smoke(ing)", "Puddle", and some more. Call me "Smoke"
                if you haven't given me a nickname before.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
